{"t":1454301.9960242,"req":"h01","event":"done","status":"answered","level":0,"steps":["classify","retrieve","loop","draft"],"answer":"The original attention divides the query\u2011key dot products by \\( \\sqrt{d_k} \\) because without this scaling the dot products can become large in magnitude (especially for large \\(d_k\\)), pushing the softmax into regions with extremely small gradients. Scaling by \\(1/\\sqrt{d_k}\\) keeps the values in a range where the softmax remains sensitive and gradients are stable[C:attention:9]. The same reasoning is reiterated: dot\u2011product attention can produce large values, so the scaling counteracts this effect and improves training stability[C:attention:10]."}
