{"t":1454362.3484399,"req":"h07","event":"done","status":"answered","level":0,"steps":["classify","retrieve","draft"],"answer":"Moshi\u2019s \u201cInner Monologue\u201d is a modeling technique that first predicts time\u2011aligned text tokens as a prefix and then generates the corresponding audio tokens from a neural audio\u2011codec residual quantizer.  By running the text\u2011to\u2011speech generation and the user\u2011speech generation in parallel streams, it removes explicit speaker turns and enables real\u2011time, full\u2011duplex spoken dialogue.  The method also allows Moshi to be repurposed as streaming TTS or streaming ASR simply by adjusting the delay between the two token types[C:moshi:1][C:moshi:15]."}
